==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Subterra Guardians''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Subterra Sentinels''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

Evolves into '''Subterra Saviors''' at level 60 using [[Catfruit]], [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Thermae is the epitome of an anti-zombie unit in a shiny package. Having enough range to counter many Zombies and a long backwards [[Omni Strike]] coverage, it can even catch zombies that have burrowed a little behind it. Its strength against Zombies is further defined by its three-part multi-hit which separates its attacks into three parts, each carrying a 1-second [[Freeze|Freeze]]. Combined with Thermae's high attack rate, it can greatly impede zombies and swiftly finish them, even if they burrow into itself. Its low speed also allows it to stay behind, catching any stray zombies that managed to avoid your frontline. Its high knockback count ensures even when overwhelmed, it could still quickly recover ground and exploit its range.

==='''True Form'''===
This True Form adds nothing beyond a small damage boost. Obviously, more damage is always good for a damage-focused unit, but it's better to invest in them if you also wish to unlock this unit's Talents or its Ultra Form.

==='''Ultra Form'''===
Off-rip, the stat buffs on Subterra Saviors are ridiculous: a 1.5x HP buff and 1.1x DPS buff are nothing to sneeze at. Subterra Sentinels was already sturdy, but now it is basically unkillable under normal circumstances. Furthermore, the uptime on its Freeze now reaches a ~63% uptime on Zombies (~58% on Relics), assuming all three hits connect, a number that many Freeze specialists like [[Frozen Rose Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Frozen Rose Cat]] and [[Hanasaka Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Ravenous Cherry]] can only dream of having.

The real star of the show here, however, is its Relic targetting. Subterra Saviors' superb performance as an anti-Zombie translates very well against Relics, standing its ground against basically every common matchup, and tanking the enemies it doesn't innately outrange. Truthfully, there's almost nothing (outside of certain Legend Bosses) that can pose a genuine threat to it with how great its survivability is. [[Ancient Magamojoe]]s, [[Iguanidae Ibilujon]]s, [[Othom]]s, you name it; Subterra Saviors can do it. This is one of the highest priority Ultra Forms to unlock when entering [[Uncanny Legends]], as it completely trivializes potentially problematic encounters with enemies like [[Relic Bun-Bun]]s and [[M. Ost]]s.

Another thing worth mentioning is the upgrade to its Omni Strike's forward pierce, which is a very welcome bonus that improves Subterra Saviors' quality of life more significantly than one would initially suspect. A peon narrowly intercepting it just as it's reaching its target no longer means the unit is guaranteed to whiff its 6.5-second attack cycle. The Ultra Form is somewhat cheap as well, only costing what basically amounts to some pocket change in terms of [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stone|Behemoth Stones]]. Be sure to unlock Subterra Saviors' Curse Immunity Talent prior to Ultra Forming them, it is effectively mandatory for optimal performance.

==='''Talents'''===
As a stat-based unit, '''Strengthen''', '''Defense Buff''' and '''Attack Buff''' are pretty good, with Strengthen having the highest priority due to Subterra Sentinels' high knockback count, which allows it to take great advantage of any extra damage as it can still reposition twice at that point. As for the other two, more damage and health are always great to have, though their steep NP cost means it's better to invest in them if you use this unit a lot and have lots of NP to share after boosting them with [[Catseye]]s.

'''Soulstrike''', just like on any other Iron Legion uber is detrimental to its usability. While on paper it may be useful thanks to its Omni-Strike, problems arise when there are actual threatening zombies up front. Combined with its long attack animation and slow speed, it'll be more detrimental than it would be helpful. Do not unlock this, as it '''cannot be disabled'''.

On the other hand, '''Curse Immune''' and '''Freeze Resist''' are not as useful. Although Curse Immune does see use in stages where Zombies are paired with these threats (such as [[Golem Sunfish]] in [[Retreat of the Living Dead]]), it's too situational to be considered worthwhile, unless going for its Ultra Form where its Relic Targeting grants better matchups. Freeze Resist, similarly, has few uses, since Zir Zeal's freeze has full uptime with its fast attack rate, while most other threats don't warrant the use of Subterra Sentinels at all, making it competely useless as well.

==='''Orb'''===
The only Orb worth using on Subterra Sentinels is a Strong Up Orb against Zombies. If you have his Ultra Form, a Strong Up Orb against Relic can be useful.

