==Trivia==
*Subterra Guardians appear to be a foil to [[Mighty Rekon Korps (Uber Rare Cat)|Orbital Platform Armageddon]].
**Both units attack via surprise ambush: Armageddon engages enemies from outer space through a portal, while the Subterra Guardians surface from deep within the Earth's crust.
**The mustachioed cat works as the "bait" for Armageddon's operations and summons them at will with a big red button, whereas the eyepatch cat appears to unknowingly send signals to the Subterra Guardians through a metal detector.
**The mustachioed cat appears calm and collected throughout Armageddon's attack animation, while the eyepatch cat loses composure and panics.
*Even if its Normal Form's description says that it Slows and causes massive damage to Zombies, it actually Freezes them and is Strong Against them. Massive damage only implies it does great damage to zombies, and does not refer to the eponymous ability.
**The Evolved Form's description says that it freezes Zombies, but still says that it has massive damage.
**Both forms' descriptions have been corrected in an unknown update.
*The excavation machines seen during Subterra Guardians' attack animation are the Grandon Mining Corps Cats. Interestingly, Thermae was added in Version 6.10, while the Grandon Mining Corps were added in [[Version 8.0 Update|Version 8.0]].
**The Subterra Sentinels' attack animation shows the [[True Form]]s of the Grandon Mining Corps, which were added in [[Version 10.6 Update|Version 10.6]], and feature different sprites. Like its prior form, Subterra Sentinels also predates the Grandon Corps True Forms, since it was added in Version 8.4.
**Subterra Saviors' attack animation hints at an Ultra Form appearance to the Grandon Mining Corps.
*The Cat is seen wearing a [[wikipedia:Fire proximity suit|Fire Proximity Suit]], used by volcanologists for protection against heat sources.
*Subterra Sentinels, [[Mighty Drednot (Uber Rare Cat)|B.C.S. Tigerclaw]], [[Mighty Carrowsell (Uber Rare Cat)|Extradimensional Envanz]], [[Mighty Bomburr (Uber Rare Cat)|NEK-02 Air Citadel]], [[Mighty Aethur Ltd. (Uber Rare Cat)|Ultra Atlantis Logistix]], and [[Mighty Deth-Troy-R (Uber Rare Cat)|Obliterator Diabolosa]] are the only six units with 6 Talents instead of the usual 5 Talents.
**Incidentally, all six of these units get [[Soulstrike]] as one of these Talents and are all from the [[Frontline Assault IRON LEGION (Gacha Event)|Iron Legion gacha]].
*In the Upgrade Menu icons for the Evolved, True, and Ultra Forms, the eyepatch cat stands in front of a different Grandon Corps unit. Those units being [[Driller Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Power Driller Cat]], [[Piledriver Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Neo Piledriver Cat]], and an Ultra-Form variant of [[Cutter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Neo Cutter Cat]].

